  "_branches": "One block per branch tenant (config/branch-groups.json). `stylists`: the founder's confirmed list of 2026-10-03, short Latin names exactly as written; `website` is the key in matrix_website config/stylists.js whose calendar the branch books into (the same calendar as the website). A stylist the website has no calendar for is written \"not-connected\", and the whole branch stays off until every one is connected. `qpay`: both branches invoice under the SAME QPay merchant (the website create-payment handler's one, mcc 7230) on the SAME login (the platform's QPAY_*, terminal DALATECH_AI), exactly as Яармаг and Core Language do (founder, 2026-10-04: no merchant or login of Парк Од's own). The ONLY difference is the bank account a branch's deposits are paid into, named in every invoice's bank_accounts. \"website\": that account is the website's config/branches.js one (Яармаг, unchanged); \"operator\": it comes from the operator's environment under the website's own names (PARKOD_QPAY_BANK_CODE, PARKOD_QPAY_ACCOUNT_NUMBER, PARKOD_QPAY_ACCOUNT_NAME: her Khan Bank account) and the branch's qpay is \"not-connected\" until all three exist; an account equal to another branch's is refused. Otgonjargal (Отгонжаргал) is back (founder, 2026-10-04): Яармаг, 1-р зэрэг, female, the website's own calendar for her. `aliases`: the Cyrillic spellings a customer may TYPE at the stylist question (never shown), exactly as the founder approved them on 2026-10-04 in each branch's «Үсчдийн нэр» (Яармаг: tara_stylist_names, «Отгонжаргал» and «Отгоо» included; Парк Од: tara_park_od_wording section 4b, byte for byte), and every former name the website still accepts for her (its `formerly`, e.g. «Batzaya»; from-website.ts refuses if one is missing). A typed name must pick exactly one stylist: the parser refuses an alias that names two stylists of the SAME branch config (each branch is its own tenant, so a typed name only ever picks within its branch); across branches none is shared either (a unit test: Яармаг's Chimgee «Чимгээ» is not Парк Од's Chimegee «Чимэгээ»).",
